{"nodes": [{"id": "src_cmakelists_chrono_build_root", "label": "Chrono src Build Root", "file_type": "code", "source_file": "src/CMakeLists.txt", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Drives all module subdirectories in a deliberate order: Chrono::Mumps must be configured before any module that may depend on Intel MKL. Requires C++17 (detected per compiler family because CMake's standard flags cannot be trusted for PGI)."}, {"id": "src_cmakelists_eigen3_dependency", "label": "Eigen3 Discovery and Configuration", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "src/CMakeLists.txt", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Tries Eigen 5.0 first, then 3.3; sets _ENABLE_EXTENDED_ALIGNED_STORAGE for MSVC 15.8+ and EIGEN_DONT_PARALLELIZE when Eigen OpenMP is off. Definitions land on the Eigen3::Eigen INTERFACE target so they reach every Chrono target."}, {"id": "src_cmakelists_amd_eigen_alignment_clamp", "label": "AMD Eigen Alignment Clamp", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "src/CMakeLists.txt", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Host-side Chrono classes hold fixed-size Eigen objects that AVX would require to be 32-byte aligned, but some allocation paths (demos, visualization, MBS coupling) do not guarantee that; in ROCm builds this aborted demo_FSI-SPH_CouetteFlow before any SPH kernel ran. Clamping EIGEN_MAX_ALIGN_BYTES/EIGEN_MAX_STATIC_ALIGN_BYTES to 16 keeps SSE-friendly vectorization without the fragile over-alignment. Deliberately keyed on CHRONO_GPU_VENDOR_RESOLVED == AMD rather than CHRONO_HIP_FOUND, because it changes the ABI of every target and must not fire on a CUDA build that merely has ROCm installed."}, {"id": "src_cmakelists_rocm_thrust_exclusion", "label": "ROCm-packaged Thrust Exclusion", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "src/CMakeLists.txt", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "A Thrust that resolved inside the ROCm tree is dropped for host-side Chrono targets in HIP builds; keyed on the resolved vendor, not on CHRONO_HIP_FOUND, so an NVIDIA build with ROCm merely present keeps its Thrust."}, {"id": "src_cmakelists_gpu_backend_layers", "label": "Three-Layer GPU Backend Resolution", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "src/CMakeLists.txt", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Layer 0 ChronoGPUVendor answers which hardware is targeted, layer 1 ChronoGPUToolchains which SDKs are usable, layer 2 ChronoGPUModule what each feature compiles as. ChronoGPUDetect must be include()d at file scope because it calls enable_language()."}, {"id": "src_cmakelists_chconfig_h_generation", "label": "ChConfig.h Generation", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "src/CMakeLists.txt", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Every enabled module and detected capability (SIMD, OpenMP, CUDA, HIP, Thrust, HDF5, YAML, gtest, gbenchmark) is turned into a #define/#undef substitution variable and configured into chrono/ChConfig.h, which is how C++ code discovers the build configuration."}, {"id": "src_cmakelists_yaml_cpp_integration", "label": "yaml-cpp FetchContent Integration", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "src/CMakeLists.txt", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Fetched from the in-tree third-party directory; sample tools are force-disabled because Chrono uses none of them and they escape the library-level warning suppression. MSVC warning pragmas are PUBLIC since yaml-cpp headers are reached through Chrono's own src/ include root where the SYSTEM include mechanism cannot mark them external. Disabled entirely on VS 2019 and older."}, {"id": "src_cmakelists_chronoconfig_cmake_export", "label": "ChronoConfig.cmake Package Export", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "src/CMakeLists.txt", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Two variants of the package config are generated, one for the build tree and one for the install tree, alongside ChronoTargets.cmake exported under the Chrono:: namespace."}], "edges": [{"source": "src_cmakelists_chrono_build_root", "target": "src_chrono_cmakelists_chrono_core", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "src/CMakeLists.txt", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "src_cmakelists_chrono_build_root", "target": "src_chrono_fsi_cmakelists_chrono_fsi", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "src/CMakeLists.txt", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "src_cmakelists_chrono_build_root", "target": "src_chrono_dem_cmakelists_chrono_dem", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "src/CMakeLists.txt", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "src_cmakelists_chrono_build_root", "target": "src_chrono_vehicle_cmakelists_chrono_vehicle", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "src/CMakeLists.txt", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "src_cmakelists_chrono_build_root", "target": "src_chrono_models_cmakelists_chrono_models", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "src/CMakeLists.txt", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "src_cmakelists_chrono_build_root", "target": "src_chrono_vehicle_cosim_cmakelists_chrono_vehicle_cosim", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source